{"title":"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the context of this problem, a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/d/c1dca7b60707b76bfa73436bfea61b882c986eec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\emph{square}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"11\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b931b4ecb324b5389d91919ee30d53b913cd5b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> block, a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/066794db7048fcf5661911c532bb08252c9c5fa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\emph{domino}$\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6c8b62c658c4d2cde679951a8b1e450d1b88b5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> block, and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/9/749fbb82f93e5c22c3e45e9dd98ae07d4a3a29d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\emph{triomino}$\" width=\"62\" height=\"11\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/0/47054764af9c891341022f5943cdd34c7a9a99ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> block. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the number of ways George can place one square, two identical dominoes, and three identical triominoes on a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/8/b1850eeb1deab131137385e5ca78be42302d1d13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> chessboard such that no two overlap, find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by 1000.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Once the pieces are placed, there will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/f/51fdd21883d6a994a77c0a968e259bcc24edd1a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20-3(3)-2(2)-1=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"18\" /> blank spaces. So, we are simply ordering <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triominoes, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dominoes, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> square, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> blank spaces. That's just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93bcd886f029433c5c6ee7efa7064f946467bfd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12!}{3!2!6!} = 55440$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"115\" height=\"38\" />, with last three digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/e/e5e674e0e21988b92844efb94e443f74d704f055.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{440}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010\">Mock AIME 1 2010</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems\">Problems</a></b>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t={{{source}}}\">Source</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2010 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2010_Problems/Problem_3\"